# Production Environment
#
# **VITE_API_BASE_URL is deliberately empty**, and emptying it is the fix rather
# than the omission. It held `https://api.mesh.enterprise.internal`, a host
# nobody owns, and `import.meta.env` bakes that value into the bundle at build
# time — so every API call in a production build went there, the proxy was never
# reached, and the screen rendered while nothing behind it answered.
#
# Nothing caught it because `.env.development` is empty and every test and every
# local run is a dev build. The production path had never been executed.
#
# Empty means the front end calls relative paths and the browser resolves them
# against the page's own origin — the host serving `dist`, which proxies `/api`
# to `agent-mesh-http`. That is the deployment written down in
# `docs/running-locally.md`, "Deploying it somewhere else".
#
# **If the absolute-URL branch is chosen instead**, this is where the origin
# goes — and then `AGENT_MESH_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` on the http server has to name
# the front end's origin, because that branch is cross-origin. The two go
# together; setting one without the other is what produced this.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
